From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: playportdev <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:26:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 83/85] ntdll, process: drop what was there only for CEF

Playport runs no CEF (its Steam client is the app's own; no steamwebhelper
is ever started), but four pieces built for Steam's CEF were still live:

- The ml433 8 GB "V8/cppgc cage" holdback at 0x7200000000, reserved at
  every boot: half of the 16 GB guest window under the furniture ceiling.
  Death's Door filled the other half 14 s in. It is now reserved only for a
  title whose madeira.cfg sets jumbo-mb (The Witcher 3, whose exact 8 GB ask
  it serves next to the jumbo hold); "[cage] no holdback" says so otherwise.
- The ml434 4 GB soft "cppgc caged heap" grant: any 4 GB reserve the kernel
  could not place was answered with unbacked address space at 0x7500000000
  or 0x7600000000, where steered arenas and placements above the ceiling
  now live. Removed; such an ask now fails as on any full address space.
- The ml462 V8 CodeRange service: every reserve-only PAGE_NOACCESS ask of
  512 MB to 513 MB went to [0x7180000000, 0x71c0000000) "near libcef's
  builtins", and was refused outright after 32 reserve/release cycles on a
  thread. Removed with its cycle tracker; such asks take the normal path.
- The steamwebhelper process gate (task #34): forced single-process CEF,
  spliced Chromium switches into its command line and refused its --type=
  children. Removed.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-06-guest-va-exhaustion.md
Offered-upstream: no
